/* Keep awake */
"settings.section.keepAwake" = "Keep Awake";
"settings.keepAwake" = "Keep the screen on; closing the lid only blanks the display — no sleep, no lock, no network loss";
"settings.keepAwake.footer" = "While on: an open lid never blanks the screen; closing the lid only turns the display off — the system stays awake, network and apps keep running, and reopening the lid returns straight to the desktop without a password. How: a virtual display named \"MeiMacPlus Keep Awake\" (1920×1080) appears in your system; on lid close the session migrates onto it, so the internal panel powers off as a display switch rather than a sleep, and no lock is raised — it is normal to see it in Display settings and in recordings/screen shares. First enable asks once for an administrator password to install a background helper. The Mac won't sleep automatically or manually while enabled — mind heat on battery; other keep-awake tools (e.g. Awayke) will fight over the same setting.";
"keepawake.error.title" = "Could not change a keep-awake setting";
